$music — music generation (ACE-Step)

SUMMARY
  Generates audio tracks from captions (prompts[]) and lyrics (texts[]).
  Supports multiple models, caption/lyrics pairing rules, and GGUF
  (ace-synth) or native PyTorch (safetensors) backends.

SYNTAX
  $music(model='st')
  $music(model=@music_models)[2]
  $music(bpm=128, guidance_scale=3, duration=30, format=wav)

INPUT
  prompts[] — caption / style description (one or many; paired with lyrics).
  texts[]   — lyrics; default [Instrumental] if empty.

OUTPUT
  sounds[] — WAV/MP3 links under op/sounds/
             Names: {timestamp}_{model}_music_{i}.{ext}
  prompts[] — cleared after generation.

ARGUMENTS
  model=     — registry name or @instruction list (externals/music/model_list.py)
  count=     — tracks per caption/lyrics pair (or use [n] suffix)
  duration=  — seconds (else model default)
  seed=      — -1 for random; else fixed / offset per variant
  steps=     — diffusion steps (else model / inference_steps default)
  format=    — output extension: wav, mp3, … (default wav)
  bpm, shift, guidance_scale, keyscale, timesignature, language, adapter,
  lm_temperature, lm_top_p, lm_cfg_scale, use_cot_caption, … — passed to ace-synth / native

MODEL NOTES
  default, xl-turbo, turbo — GGUF under models/ace-step-1.5/, ace-synth
  st — safetensors HF bundle under models/ace-step-1.5_st/, native PyTorch
  See model_list.py for per-model duration, steps, adapters.

BACKENDS (ACESTEP_BACKEND)
  synth (default) — ace-synth CLI + GGUF weights
  native — pip install ace-step from GitHub (ACE-Step-1.5)
  api — ACESTEP_API_URL HTTP service
  auto — per-model preferred_backend

ENVIRONMENT
  ACESTEP_SYNTH_BIN, ACESTEP_DOWNLOAD_BIN, ACESTEP_CHECKPOINTS_DIR,
  MODELS_PATH, HF_HOME, ACESTEP_DIT_GGUF, …
  AH_EMULATE_MUSIC=1 — short placeholder beep WAV.

EXAMPLE
  @track: (@caption, @lyrics_text) -> $music(model='st')
  @testing: $input_json('…/output.json') -> $music(model=@music_models)

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes.
